  "rationale": "The source body label (retained-agenda, provider-player) names the convened body as a joint meeting of the Board of Trustees of Eagle Mountain-Saginaw ISD and the Fort Worth City Council for the April 25, 2016 meeting at Hollenstein Career Tech Center. The agenda and chapter index (native-source-chapters) corroborate dual convening and governance: Board President Dick Elkins calls the meeting, gives the welcome and announcements, and ISD business is conducted (Reports of the Superintendent, EMS ISD demographic report, EMS ISD economic development initiative, State of the District, career and technology initiatives with Superintendent Jim Chadwell and staff), while Fort Worth Mayor Betsy Price delivers the welcome, Mayor's Report on Education, City of Fort Worth items (Master Thoroughfare Plan) and Mayor's Announcements. Both named participants are therefore proven as joint conveners, not merely attendees, and under the joints rule each proven participant shares the recording in its configured feed. The existing feed fort-worth-tx-emsisd-board-joint-meetings is explicitly described as source-scoped joint proceedings of the EMSISD Board and Fort Worth Council with original whole recordings retained, making it the configured feed for the ISD Board's participation; fort-worth-tx-city-council is the configured feed for the Council's participation. Identity follows the convened bodies, not the venue (Hollenstein Career Tech Center is an ISD facility) and not the hosting on Fort Worth's Granicus portal, which alone would not make this solely a Council meeting. The opening ceremony is a single agenda item within a substantive joint business meeting, so the ceremonies exclusion does not remove the recording from body feeds. No other suspected participants exist and no ownership proof is missing, so no unresolved or unconfigured entry is needed."
